+        "statement": "`Registry.save` writes the entire in-memory slice (`internal/repos/registry.go`), so a second running configserver holding a pre-delete slice resurrects a deleted entry via last-writer-wins. The fix is read-modify-write on save (re-read the on-disk state and merge), not IPC coordination between the two writers. Related: cache invalidation must key on a data-derived fingerprint, not a TTL — `DropBranches` leaving an entry's pre-removal fingerprint stale is what made the next load mismatch and re-scan."
